Sure! Below is a minimal example of an “interactive rotating card” you can drop straight into your project.  
It uses only **HTML + CSS** (no JavaScript) and works in all modern browsers.

---

### 1️⃣ Markup

```html
<div class="card">
    <div class="card__face card__face--front">
        <!-- Front side content -->
        <h2>Front</h2>
        <p>This is the front of the card.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card__face card__face--back">
        <!-- Back side content -->
        <h2>Back</h2>
        <p>This is the back of the card.</p>
    </div>
</div>
```

* `card` – container that holds both faces.  
* `card__face` – common styling for each face.  
* `card__face--front / --back` – differentiate the two sides.

---

### 2️⃣ Styles

```css
/* Basic reset */
*, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }

/* Card container */
.card {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
    margin: 50px auto;            /* Center horizontally */
}

/* Common face styles */
.card__face {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide backside when rotated away */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: #fff;
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: transform 0.8s ease; /* Smooth rotation */
}

/* Front face */
.card__face--front {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff7e5f, #feb47b);
}

/* Back face – initially rotated 180° so it’s hidden */
.card__face--back {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #43cea2, #185a9d);
    transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* Start flipped */
}

/* Hover effect – flip the whole card */
.card:hover .card__face--front,
.card:hover .card__face--back {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* Flip both faces together */
}
```

#### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| 1 | `.card` sets a 3‑D space with `perspective`. |
| 2 | Each face is absolutely positioned on top of one another. |
| 3 | `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the backside when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| 4 | On hover, we rotate **both** faces 180°. Because the back face was already rotated 180°, it ends up facing the viewer while the front flips away. |

---

### 3️⃣ Tweaking & Customization

| Property | Purpose | Example |
|----------|---------|---------|
| `perspective` | Depth of the 3‑D effect | `800px`, `1200px` |
| `transition-duration` | Speed of the flip | `0.6s`, `1.2s` |
| `transform-origin` | Pivot point of rotation | `center`, `top left` |
| `border-radius` | Rounded corners | `20px` |
| `background` | Color scheme | Use images, gradients, solid colors |

Feel free to replace the gradient backgrounds with images or solid colors, adjust the size, or change the rotation axis (`rotateX`, `rotateZ`) for different visual effects.

---

### 4️⃣ Full Working Demo

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Insert the CSS from section 2 here */
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="card">
    <div class="card__face card__face--front">
        <h2>Front</h2>
        <p>This is the front of the card.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card__face card__face--back">
        <h2>Back</h2>
        <p>This is the back of the card.</p>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

Open this file in a browser, hover over the card, and watch it flip!

Happy coding!
